    │   in pymodbus vs slaveaddress in minimalmodbus)
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── All three libraries provide Modbus master/client functionality capable 
        of reading holding registers over TCP (or serial) from a meter/PLC. 
        pyModbusTCP is a close functional match (pure TCP client with 
        read_holding_registers-style calls). minimalmodbus is primarily 
        designed for serial/RS-485 Modbus RTU but does support Modbus TCP via 
        minimalmodbus.Instrument with mode='tcp', so it is a plausible but 
        weaker substitute for this specific TCP use case.

