Equivalence Groups Found
└── synchronous HTTP client for REST calls (session-based get/post with 
    status/error handling)
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, session.post, r.raise_for_status, 
    │   r.json, r.status_code
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client vs requests.Session: constructor and default 
    │   behaviors differ slightly (e.g., redirect following defaults, 
    │   connection pooling config); Timeout handling differs: requests uses a 
    │   float/tuple, httpx uses httpx.Timeout object or float with different 
    │   semantics; Exception hierarchies differ: requests.exceptions.HTTPError 
    │   vs httpx.HTTPStatusError/HTTPError; httpx.Client must be closed or used
    │   as a context manager for proper resource cleanup, unlike 
    │   requests.Session which is more lenient
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses requests.Session as an injectable HTTP client performing 
        synchronous GET/POST calls with timeout, raise_for_status, and json() 
        parsing. httpx provides a sync httpx.Client with an almost identical 
        API (get/post/raise_for_status/json), making it a viable drop-in 
        replacement for this usage pattern. urllib3 is excluded because 
        requests is built on top of it (dependency chain rule), and aiohttp is 
        excluded because it is async-only and would require rewriting the 
        entire client to async/await, not just call-site substitution.

